th the cost of living and  many of them are working in the public  sector and they're facing pay cuts  everybody who works in in health  education care council services have all  seen pay suppression  and the only way to break that cycle is  to get paid deals that break it now all  money in circulation comes from all of  us  so somebody is paying for every service  or product that you buy  but if we have continual  price suppression you will have  continual hyper profit and there's got  to be a balance in the society between  profit and income we're not getting  enough income and they're getting too  much profit  that you're talking about here  well last year in the railway  industry  the rolling stock companies network rail  subcontractors  and the train operating companies made  500 million pounds of direct profit  that's that's a fact is in their books  last year on rail  last year on rail the first group which  is one of the major  shareholders and train operating  companies made 108 million pound out of  rail alone  they have been subject to a takeover bid  of 1.2 billion  go ahead who's one of the other  companies are also subject to a takeover  bid so somebody thinks they're going to  make profits out of rail because private  equity companies from abroad are coming  here to buy these companies  while they're managing directors are  earning millions the cheap the top  earner in network rail earned 1.2  million pounds in salary during covid  his chief financial operator uh  executive earned nearly half a million  pound each year during covid all of  these executives that we're dealing with  are on salaries in excess of three  hundred and fifty thousand pounds a year  somebody's making money out of the  railways just not our members so it  should be there should be some kind of  windfall tax like we've seen in the old  well i'd like the windfall tax to be a  windfall for our members through their  wages that would be a start someone's  gotta pay for that additio